# Derived by hand from Semantics ch. 4 ("Binding groups and cycles": the order of a group's lines decides positions and nothing else; a block's build is one tick's), ch. 8 (a widget application is transparent) and ruling TC (places counted as built): a `let` gives a bundle another name (Type System ch. 2, "Bundles"); the first label is 0 and reads the arm's result; the loud arm builds 1, so the button is 2; the soft arm builds none, so it is 1.
test loud

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Label(text="step 10")
    1: Ui.Label(text="x")
    2: Ui.Button(label="go")

